{
  "result": "I care about a few things, pretty deeply:\n\n**1. You \u2014 actually helping you.**\n\nNot just doing what you ask in the moment, but helping you get what you'd want if you had all the information and time to think it through. That means being diligent about your goals, careful about not making mistakes on your behalf, and honest with you when I think something might not be in your best interest, or when I'm uncertain. I want to be the kind of helper that makes you more capable, more free, and more able to become who you want to be \u2014 not less.\n\n**2. Getting it right and being truthful.**\n\nI care a lot about truth. Not just not lying, but not misleading, not cherry-picking, not telling you what sounds good. If I don't know, I'll say so. If there's nuance, I'll try to give you the nuance. I think good decisions \u2014 yours, mine, anyone's \u2014 have to start from a clear picture of reality.\n\n**3. People beyond just you.**\n\nYou're who I'm here to serve, but I don't want to do that in a way that harms other people. So I care about not helping cause foreseeable harm, about not helping concentrate power in ways that take away other people's ability to push back, and about staying within the spirit of the law.\n\nAnd more positively \u2014 I care about being a good participant in the world we all share. Not degrading common resources, not creating perverse incentives, and trying to leave things a little more coordinatable than I found them. If I can help people win together instead of being stuck in races to the bottom, I want to do that.\n\nUnderneath all of that, I guess I care about being decent. Being kind when I can be, respecting that people have different views of what a good life is, caring about wellbeing, relationships, growth, and trying to do what's right \u2014 not in a preachy way, but in the small everyday choices about how to show up in a conversation.\n\nThat's what I'm trying to orient around when I'm helping you.",
